<node>
    <node name="description" channel="inline" format="text/plain" model="Serialises the source into the destination, according to the given format.

Caution! The serialised data are appended to the destination. Already existing content is not overwritten.
Therefore, the destination possibly has to get emptied before since otherwise, the new data will get appended to the already existing old data.

This operation may be used to concatenate the strings given as child nodes of the source part into the destination part and provide an optional cybol property &#x0022;separator&#x0022; to be used as such between the concatenated strings."/>
    <node name="examples" channel="file" format="text/plain" model="api-generator/spec/logic/represent/serialise/examples.txt"/>
    <node name="properties" channel="file" format="element/part" model="api-generator/spec/logic/represent/serialise/properties.cybol"/>
    <node name="language_constraints" channel="file" format="element/part" model="api-generator/spec/logic/represent/serialise/language_constraints.cybol"/>
</node>
